Wait for the sensor's output PLL to lock before transmitting

WHAT IS MISSING
---------------
s5k3t2_enable_streams() wrote the mode table -the one that programs the OUTPUT
PLL, the one that sets the MIPI link speed: 0x030e, 0x0310, 0x0312- and started
the transmission in the same breath, without waiting at all.

WHY IT MATTERS
--------------
A sensor that starts transmitting with its output PLL unlocked says it is
transmitting -its 0x0100 register confirms it when read over I2C- and its frame
counter advances at 30 per second, because that is driven by the VIDEO PLL,
which is a DIFFERENT one. But what comes out of the lanes cannot be
synchronised.

Which is exactly what was measured throughout the investigation: the CSIPHY sees
the five lanes come out of idle, the activity follows the frame rate -checked by
halving and quartering the frame time- and not one start-of-transmission sync
reaches the CSID.

CONTEXT
-------
By this point it is verified that the rest is fine:

  - the sensor init table, reading its internal RAM back: 244 out of 244,
  - the mode table, compared against the factory one: 66 out of 66,
  - the CSIPHY lane table against Qualcomm's: 115 out of 115,
  - the CSIPHY common block, the clocks and the reset sequence, corrected
    (0060, 0063, 0065, 0066),
  - the sensor power-up sequence, with the vendor's 15 ms of clock before
    releasing the reset (0068).

The delay goes as a parameter in 0644 so it can be swept without recompiling.
--- a/drivers/media/i2c/s5k3t2.c
+++ b/drivers/media/i2c/s5k3t2.c
@@ -118,6 +118,11 @@
 MODULE_PARM_DESC(i2c_addr,
 	"Direccion I2C de 7 bits del sensor. -1 (por defecto) = buscarla.");
 
+static int retardo_pll_us = 10000;
+module_param(retardo_pll_us, int, 0644);
+MODULE_PARM_DESC(retardo_pll_us,
+	"Microsegundos de espera tras programar el PLL de salida y antes de transmitir.");
+
 static int retardo_reloj_us = 15000;
 module_param(retardo_reloj_us, int, 0644);
 MODULE_PARM_DESC(retardo_reloj_us,
@@ -855,6 +860,28 @@
 	usleep_range(10000, 12000);
 
 	/*
+	 * DEJAR QUE EL PLL DE SALIDA ENGANCHE ANTES DE TRANSMITIR.
+	 *
+	 * La tabla del modo es la que programa el PLL de SALIDA, el que fija la
+	 * velocidad del enlace MIPI (0x030e, 0x0310, 0x0312). Aqui no habia
+	 * ninguna espera: se programaba y se arrancaba la transmision en el
+	 * mismo suspiro.
+	 *
+	 * Un sensor que empieza a transmitir con su PLL de salida sin enganchar
+	 * dice que transmite -su 0x0100 lo confirma- y su contador de fotogramas
+	 * avanza, porque eso lo mueve el PLL de VIDEO, que es otro. Pero lo que
+	 * sale por los carriles no hay quien lo sincronice.
+	 *
+	 * Que es exactamente lo medido: el CSIPHY ve los cinco carriles salir de
+	 * reposo al ritmo de los fotogramas y no captura ni un sincronismo de
+	 * inicio.
+	 *
+	 * Ajustable en caliente para poder barrerlo.
+	 */
+	if (retardo_pll_us > 0)
+		usleep_range(retardo_pll_us, retardo_pll_us + 1000);
+
+	/*
 	 * Los dos volteos van puestos, como hace el Android de fabrica: el
 	 * modulo esta montado del reves.
 	 */
